-**Formulas:**
-The core pipeline implements the emission-absorption optical model using front-to-back compositing. For each sample $i$ along a ray, accumulated color $C'$ and opacity $\alpha'$ update as:
-$$
-C'_{i} = C'_{i-1} + (1 - \alpha'_{i-1}) \alpha_i C_i
-$$
-$$
-\alpha'_{i} = \alpha'_{i-1} + (1 - \alpha'_{i-1}) \alpha_i
-$$
-where $\alpha_i$ is the opacity derived from the sampled density, and $C_i$ is the sample color.
+**Memory Architecture Optimization**
+A specific memory architecture uses buffers and a pre-fetch mechanism to enhance bandwidth utilization [S1]. This increases the sample processing efficiency ($P_s$) to 0.2, at the cost of a higher voxel re-fetch factor ($V$) [S1]. In large multi-module configurations, sample processing efficiency per module may decrease due to network overhead [S1].
 
